.\" karvi-job(1): the manual page of karvi's job word. Written by hand except
.\" the regions between the markers, which tools/mangen rewrites from the
.\" word's help text (make generate).
.TH KARVI-JOB 1 "" "karvi"
.\" Paths and options are not hyphenated, and lines are not stretched.
.nh
.ds AD l
.ad l
.SH NAME
karvi\-job \- list the jobs, or follow or cancel one by its ID
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" BEGIN GENERATED SYNOPSIS: tools/mangen from internal/cli; edit there
\fBkarvi\fR \fBjob list\fR [\-\-last N] [\-\-failed] [\-\-target NAME]... [\-\-operator NAME]...
[\-\-format text|json]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBjob follow\fR JOB\-ID [\-\-format text|jsonl|json] [\-\-echo] [\-\-border | \-\-noborder]
.br
\fBkarvi\fR \fBjob cancel\fR JOB\-ID [\-\-reason TEXT] [\-\-follow] [\-\-format text|json]
.\" END GENERATED SYNOPSIS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" BEGIN GENERATED DESCRIPTION: tools/mangen from internal/cli; edit there
.PP
job lists the jobs of the output root, or operates on one accepted job, named
by the job ID of its receipt (the ID a detached run prints, and job list and
karvi watch show). No job verb launches a daemon.
.PP
list reads each job's folder and needs no daemon or credential: in shared
mode every job of the shared tree, every operator's, in individual mode the
operator's own. It shows the newest 20 jobs, newest first by job ID, whatever
their day: JOB\-ID, TIME (the job's duration), STATUS, OPERATOR (the owner of
the job's summary), MODE (cmd, run, or crun), DONE as done/total, FAIL, and
TARGET, the devices, as many whole as the terminal's width leaves and the rest
counted as +N; to a pipe or a file nothing is cut. An unfinished job shows
STATUS unfinished, TIME blank, and u, unknown, in DONE and FAIL; ? flags a
folder whose summary cannot be read. \-\-last N lists N rows, 0 every job kept.
\-\-failed keeps the finished jobs whose exit is not 0. \-\-target NAME keeps the
jobs that reached a matching device, NAME taken as run's \-\-target takes it (a
glob, repeatable, a leading ! removing the devices it matches), and lists one
row per such device: JOB\-ID, TIME, OPERATOR, MODE, OUTCOME (the device's own),
and DEVICE. \-\-operator NAME, repeatable, keeps that operator's jobs. Each
filter judges a job before \-\-last counts it. \-\-format json prints an array of
the rows: each job's summary fields, its folder's path, and its operator.
.PP
follow renders the job's records from its beginning as the foreground run
would have, live until the job ends or at once for a job that has ended,
ends as the run's display ends (the footer, and a collection's line), and
exits with the job's own exit.
\-\-format, \-\-echo, \-\-border, and \-\-noborder mean what they mean for run.
Ctrl\-C stops only the follow; the job continues.
.PP
cancel stops the job and leaves every other job running; the daemon answers
at once and the job's unfinished work is recorded cancelled (exit 113).
\-\-reason TEXT is recorded with the request. \-\-follow waits for the job's end
and exits with the job's own exit. A job that already ended is reported with
its outcome; an unknown job ID is job_unknown. \-\-help shows this text.
.\" END GENERATED DESCRIPTION
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B karvi job list
The newest 20 jobs, every member's in shared mode, fitted to the terminal.
.TP
.B karvi job list \-\-failed \-\-last 0
Every job kept that ended with an exit other than 0.
.TP
.B karvi job list \-\-target "core\-*" \-\-target "!core\-lab*"
The jobs that reached a device named core\-*, one row per such device,
leaving out the core\-lab devices.
.TP
.B karvi job follow 261003\-143005\-00
Render a detached job from its beginning; it exits with the job's exit.
.TP
.B karvi job follow 261003\-143005\-00 \-\-format jsonl
The job's records and its summary, one JSON document per line.
.TP
.B karvi job cancel 261003\-143005\-00 \-\-reason "wrong change window" \-\-follow
Stop it, record why, and wait for its end (exit 113).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR karvi (1),
.BR karvi\-run (1),
.BR karvi\-watch (1)
